  "body": "[§12.2.4.10 Tag name state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#tag-name-state) seems to be missing a handler for U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN. All other [CSS whitespace characters](http://www.w3.org/TR/css3-selectors/#whitespace) terminate the tag name, and the latest version of every current browser (Android, Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Internet Explorer, iOS, Opera, Safari, Windows Phone, and Yandex) already treats carriage return accordingly: http://jsfiddle.net/fjs6do6z/\n\nCurrent text:\n\n> <dl><dt>U+0009 CHARACTER TABULATION (tab)</dt>\n> <dt>U+000A LINE FEED (LF)</dt>\n> <dt>U+000C FORM FEED (FF)</dt>\n> <dt>U+0020 SPACE</dt>\n> <dd>Switch to the before attribute name state.</dd></dl>\n",
